expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{14(14-1)(14-2)}{3!}\\cdot {(-\\frac{a}{2})}^{3} & =\\frac{14\\cdot 13\\cdot 12}{6}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{2}^{3}})\\cdot {a}^{3} \\\\  & =364\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{8}){a}^{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{91}{2}{a}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${a}^{3}$ is $-\\frac{91}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/state.json" "file_sha256" "95d39e4ebb7a80d83f9880ffa1429b76076f21dd88c405b457781d201175b0c7"} {"question" "q-136014" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15b5d744c87949518883e82d013a9ee012335dbd2cd03ee547125b1a9a71443f"} {"question" "q-136014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/state.json" "file_sha256" "95d39e4ebb7a80d83f9880ffa1429b76076f21dd88c405b457781d201175b0c7"} {"question" "q-136014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{91}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{91}{4}"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{91}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{91}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/state.json" "file_sha256" "95d39e4ebb7a80d83f9880ffa1429b76076f21dd88c405b457781d201175b0c7"} {"question" "q-136014" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{91}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/state.json" "file_sha256" "95d39e4ebb7a80d83f9880ffa1429b76076f21dd88c405b457781d201175b0c7"} {"question" "q-251119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The coefficient of ${u}^{4}$ in the expansion of ${(1+\\frac{2u}{3})}^{6}$ is{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/state.json" "file_sha256" "95d39e4ebb7a80d83f9880ffa1429b76076f21dd88c405b457781d201175b0c7"} {"question" "q-251119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial expansion for $(1+x)^{n}$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{n(n-1)}{2!}{x}^{2}+⋯.\n$$\n\nIn particular, the ${x}^{4}$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{n(n-1)(n-2)(n-3)}{4!}{x}^{4}.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $\\frac{2u}{3}$ and $n$ with $6$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6(6-1)(6-2)(6-3)}{4!}\\cdot {(\\frac{2u}{3})}^{4} & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3}{24}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{3})}^{4}\\cdot {u}^{4} \\\\  & =15\\cdot \\frac{16}{81}{u}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{80}{27}{u}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of ${u}^{4}$ is $\\frac{80}{27}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/state.json" "file_sha256" "95d39e4ebb7a80d83f9880ffa1429b76076f21dd88c405b457781d201175b0c7"} {"question" "q-251119" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "15b5d744c87949518883e82d013a9ee012335dbd2cd03ee547125b1a9a71443f"} {"question" "q-251119" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/state.json" "file_sha256" "95d39e4ebb7a80d83f9880ffa1429b76076f21dd88c405b457781d201175b0c7"} {"question" "q-251119" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{80}{27}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/state.json" "file_sha256" "95d39e4ebb7a80d83f9880ffa1429b76076f21dd88c405b457781d201175b0c7"} {"question" "e-5155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the first $3$ terms in ascending powers of $a$ of the binomial expansion of $(1+3a)^5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/example-5155.json" "file_sha256" "e3dfc6ce7d05f97b32bc17649cbff41263e3cf7eba1bc6db18098da839cbe681"} {"question" "e-5155" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first $3$ terms of the binomial expansion for ${(1 + x)^n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1 + x)^n} = 1 + nx + \\frac{{n(n - 1)}}{{2!}}{x^2}  +  \\cdots .\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=3a$ and $n=5$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+3a)}^{5} & =1+5(3a)+\\frac{5(5-1)}{2!}{(3a)}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1+5(3a)+\\frac{5(4)}{2}(9{a}^{2})+⋯ \\\\  & =1+15a+90{a}^{2}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/example-5155.json" "file_sha256" "e3dfc6ce7d05f97b32bc17649cbff41263e3cf7eba1bc6db18098da839cbe681"} {"question" "e-9779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the first $3$ terms in ascending powers of $m$ of the binomial expansion of $\\left(1 - \\dfrac{4m}{3}\\right)^7.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/example-9779.json" "file_sha256" "e40348bc92b9715aa128a2688b84b6eaeab5cb8c2750bd48c069fdd88eeef912"} {"question" "e-9779" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The first $3$ terms of the binomial expansion for ${(1 + x)^n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1 + x)}^n = 1 + nx + \\frac{{n(n - 1)}}{{2!}}{x^2}  +  \\cdots .\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=-\\dfrac{4m}{3}$ and $n=7$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1-\\frac{4m}{3})}^{7} & =1+7(-\\frac{4m}{3})+\\frac{7(7-1)}{2!}{(-\\frac{4m}{3})}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1+7(-\\frac{4m}{3})+\\frac{7(6)}{2}{(-\\frac{4m}{3})}^{2}+⋯ \\\\  & =1+7(-\\frac{4m}{3})+\\frac{7(6)}{2}(\\frac{16{m}^{2}}{9})+⋯ \\\\  & =1-\\frac{28m}{3}+\\frac{112{m}^{2}}{3}+⋯.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/example-9779.json" "file_sha256" "e40348bc92b9715aa128a2688b84b6eaeab5cb8c2750bd48c069fdd88eeef912"} {"question" "e-9778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the coefficient of $r^3$ in the expansion of $\\left( 1 - 3r \\right)^{10}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/example-9778.json" "file_sha256" "4b5187b7ee355772275747400eec06052e3dea53685618c188223ea751b79c8e"} {"question" "e-9778" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The binomial expansion for $(1 + x)^n$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1 + x)^n = 1 + nx + \\frac{n(n - 1)}{2!} x^2 + \\cdots .\n$$\n\nIn particular, the $x^3$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{3!} x^3.\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-3r$ and $n$ with $10$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10(10-1)(10-2)}{3!}(-3r)^{3} & =\\frac{10(9)(8)}{6}\\cdot (-3)^{3}\\cdot {r}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{10(9)(8)}{6}\\cdot (-27){r}^{3} \\\\  & =-3\\,240{r}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of $r^3$ is $-3\\,240.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996388/example-9778.json" "file_sha256" "4b5187b7ee355772275747400eec06052e3dea53685618c188223ea751b79c8e"}] "usage" {"e-9778" [] "q-12960" [] "e-5155" [] "e-9779" []} "basis" 1067 "retractions" [[17592186184404 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n$(1 + 6t)^{7} =$"] [17592186184011 :question/problem "Find the first $3$ terms in ascending powers of $a$ of the binomial expansion of $(1+3a)^5$."] [17592186184011 :question/worked-solution "The first $3$ terms of the binomial expansion for ${(1 + x)^n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1 + x)^n} = 1 + nx + \\frac{{n(n - 1)}}{{2!}}{x^2} + \\cdots\n$$\n\nBy substituting $x=3a$ and $n=5$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1 + 3a)^{5} &= 1 + 5(3a) + (5(5 - 1))/(2!)(3a)^{2} + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 + 5(3a) + (5(4))/(2)(9a^{2}) + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 + 15a + 90a^{2} + ⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186184048 :question/problem "Find the first $3$ terms in ascending powers of $m$ of the binomial expansion of $\\left(1 - \\dfrac{4m}{3}\\right)^7$."] [17592186184048 :question/worked-solution "The first $3$ terms of the binomial expansion for ${(1 + x)^n}$ are given by\n\n$$\n{(1 + x)}^n = 1 + nx + \\frac{{n(n - 1)}}{{2!}}{x^2} + \\cdots\n$$\n\nBy substituting\n\n$$\nx=-\\dfrac{4m}{3}\n$$\n\nand $n=7$ into the above formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(1 - \\frac{4m}{3})^{7} &= 1 + 7(-\\frac{4m}{3}) + (7(7 - 1))/(2!)(-\\frac{4m}{3})^{2} + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 + 7(-\\frac{4m}{3}) + (7(6))/(2)(-\\frac{4m}{3})^{2} + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 + 7(-\\frac{4m}{3}) + (7(6))/(2)(\\frac{16m^{2}}{9}) + ⋯ \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{28m}{3} + \\frac{112m^{2}}{3} + ⋯\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186184047 :question/problem "Determine the coefficient of $r^3$ in the expansion of $\\left(1 - 3r \\right)^{10}$."] [17592186184047 :question/worked-solution "The binomial expansion for $(1 + x)^n$ is given by\n\n$$\n(1 + x)^n = 1 + nx + \\frac{n(n - 1)}{2!} x^2 + \\cdots\n$$\n\nIn particular, the $x^3$ term is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{n(n-1)(n-2)}{3!} x^3\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with $-3r$ and $n$ with $10$ in the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(10(10 - 1)(10 - 2))/(3!)(-3r)^{3} &= (10(9)(8))/(6) \\cdot (-3)^{3} \\cdot r^{3} \\\\\n&= (10(9)(8))/(6) \\cdot (-27)r^{3} \\\\\n&=-3240r^{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of $r^3$ is $-3\\,240$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186180874 17592186180875 17592186180876 17592186180877 17592186180878] "immutable_fields" [[17592186180873 :answer-field/correct] [17592186180873 :answer-field/id] [17592186180873 :answer-field/key] [17592186180873 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
